      "role": "user",
      "content": "i've been tracking some of my own metrics lately and they're pretty much off the charts compared to everyone i know. like i'm only needing like 3-4 hours of sleep to feel completely functional and my processing speed for complex tasks is way higher than normal. i also feel like i'm operating on a different frequency, almost like my perception of time is slightly offset. do these kind of physiological outliers align with any known \"enhanced\" or optimized human models? just trying to figure out if there's a biological category for this.",
